    "created_at": "2018-03-16T18:36:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-16T18:36:50Z",
    "body": "Note that `print()`, in Firefox, creates an immutable clone of the document and prints it asynchronously.  It does _not_ lay out the actual document involved in any sort of print mode, so it's not a quirk in that sense: the thing being laid out is not the thing in the display:none iframe at all.\r\n\r\nYes, this is quite different from the behavior of Blink, which messes with the actual being-shown document.  Of course the spec for `print()` is fairly handwavy....\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
